 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Lifeline Event Medics\nBookings Office\n\n2027-03-01\n\nDear Ellis Grant,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Lakeshore Charity Run 10K on 2027-06-06. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the rowing club, in place by 08:45, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference EV-12671.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nMaria Ostrowski\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Lakeshore Charity Run 10K - crowd notes\nSunday 6 June 2027 / contact Ellis Grant 555-0134\ntotal 850 incl 850 runners. Few people come just to watch.\n\nhired radio or 2 last time for start team, useful. short briefing for early arrivals. no complaints from runners\n\nVIEWING\n3 barriered areas: finish the pavilion, turn at Riverside Path, start the rowing club. approx 1150 total @ 2 per sqm. over expected numbers\n\nSTART\nall start together 10:00 after warm-up + countdown. popular w/ runners\n\nSTEWARDS\nclub vols + family helpers, event t-shirts. around all day\n\nEXIT\nrunners one-way funnel to recovery, out north gate. spectators 2 marked exits, steward on each. clear in 25 mins\n\nCONTROL\nEllis Grant at control w/ radio to all supervisors. can hold wave, stop race, use PA. sups call in if area getting full\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERT OF INS.   REF AG-90144\nMeridian Mutual Insurance   POL NO EL-939815\nINSURED ....... Lakeshore Striders\nRISK LOCATION .. Kingsway Gardens\nFROM .......... June 5, 2027\nTO ............ June 7, 2027\nINDEMNITY ..... $5,000,000\nACTIVITY ...... Foot race (Lakeshore Charity Run 10K)\nISSUED ........ March 1, 2027\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Lakeshore Charity Run 10K - medical notes\nSunday 6 June 2027 / gun 10:00 / 850 runners / 10K\ncontact Ellis Grant 555-0134\nAn ambulance from Lifeline Event Medics is on site for the race; the paperwork is attached.\n\nFIRST AID\ncommittee members w/ work first aid certs. kit at HQ tent + kit in lead car\n\nWEATHER / WATER\nwater every 2.5k. forecast check -48h and -2h. >28C earlier start or shorter course. >32C cancel. foil + warm tent at finish if cold/wet\n\nHOSPITAL\ncall 911 if needed, paramedics handle it from there\n\nbg: committee done this race yrs. one long time member is retired paramedic but runs race herself, not on duty\n\nCOMMS\nradios on medical channel at all posts + bikes, phones backup. amb calls go via medical lead, who gives crew the barrier to come to\n\nLEAD\nrace director + committee\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "RACE PLAN\nLakeshore Charity Run 10K | Sunday 6 June 2027\nOrganiser: Lakeshore Striders\nRace director: Ellis Grant\nReference: AG-20054\n\nOverview\nThe Lakeshore Charity Run 10K is a 10K race of 10 km for 850 entrants, based in the Kingsway Gardens area of Port Halden. The start is at 10:00 and the course closes at 12:00.\n\nCourse\nThe course stays entirely on the Pier Promenade and the Riverside Path, away from the highway, and no road is closed for the race. The finish is at the pavilion.\n\nCourse dimensions\nThe Pier Promenade is a surfaced path about 3.5 m wide, with a railing on one side and a retaining wall on the other. The Riverside Path section is about 2.5 m wide and passes under two low bridges. Runners can go two or three abreast at most, and the start pens have to be strung along the path.\n\nSupport\nEntrants collect numbers from the rowing club from one hour before the start. Timing is by chip, with mats at the start and finish. Results are posted on the Lakeshore website the same day.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "1 March 2027\n\nEvents Office\nCity of Port Halden\n\nDear Events Officer,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nWe are applying for a street race permit for the Lakeshore Charity Run 10K on Sunday 6 June 2027. We expect 850 runners over 10K, starting at 10:00 in the Kingsway Gardens area. The completed form and the attachments (ambulance_agreement.txt, crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt) are enclosed.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nEllis Grant\nVolunteer Coordinator, Lakeshore Striders\nellis@lakeshorestriders.example / 555-0134\n",
